 are opt-in, the default is unchanged, the blind-clone wiring matches the intent, and the README and TODO text describe the code as written. I found two wording mismatches in tests and one unguarded claim, all minor.\n\n**Mismatches**\n\n1. **Test title overclaims (`stage-tests`, read).** The test at `test/gud.test.ts:782` is titled \"a bare review runs the same three stages\", but it passes `--stage bugs,adversarial,mutate` explicitly and never tests a bare review. The default is actually guarded by the next test (`test/gud.test.ts:793`), which calls `dry(dir, ['wip'])` with no `--stage` and expects `bugs, honesty, improve`. Rename the first test or drop the claim from its title.\n2. **Vague scratch-path reference (`stage-prompts`, read).** `mutatePrompt` says the backup goes in \"the scratch directory named at the top of this prompt\" (`src/stages.ts:157`). The scratch path is actually in the preamble from `preamble()` in `src/commands/review.ts:24`, which is prepended ahead of the prompt. It works in the full message, but \"the top of this prompt\" is loose. Naming the preamble would be clearer.\n3. **Confusing test name (`stage-tests`, read).** The title \"a report without REPRODUCED lines is still recorded (the prompt demanded them)\" reads as if the recording depends on the prompt. The test only checks that a stub report with no `REPRODUCED:` lines is recorded.\n\n**Verified claims**\n\n- **Opt-in default is guarded (verified).** I set `DEFAULT_STAGES` to add `'adversarial'` in `src/stages.ts`. The `wip runs bugs` and `opt-in` tests failed (`actual: [bugs, honesty, improve, adversarial]`). I restored the file and confirmed it with `cmp`.\n- **Blind-clone mapping is guarded (verified).** I removed `'mutate'` from `BLIND_STAGES`. The mutate prompt test failed on `glosses: none`. I restored the file and confirmed it with `cmp`.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n4. **Verdict wording for the new stages (read).** git-gloss's `WORDS` table in `node_modules/@ok-ggwp/git-gloss/dist/reviews.js:292` has entries only for `bugs`, `improve` and `default`. Adversarial and mutate summaries therefore fall back to \"no issues\" / \"issues found\". The TODO already records this, so it is acknowledged rather than hidden.\n5. **Prompt-only enforcement (read).** The \"no network\" and \"restore with cmp\" rules, and the absence of any post-run check that the clone was restored or that `REPRODUCED:` lines were really run, are acknowledged in the TODO. Mutate also runs the repository's own tests in direct (non-sandbox) mode by default. The README says to add `--sandbox` for untrusted code, which is the real control. This is documented, not a hidden risk.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
